-- Deployment-specific IDs — copy to `db/seed/local-ids.sql` only if you need it.
--
-- `local-ids.sql` is gitignored, and `db/migrate.sh` applies it after the
-- migrations when it exists.
--
-- Since the pilot build there is almost nothing left to put here:
--   - Google Calendar is gone (migration 012 dropped its columns).
--   - Slack is gone (removed 2026-11-08; migration 019 dropped its columns).
--   - Instagram accounts are connected by the studio itself through IG Connect
--     (`python3 workflows/build/ig_connect_link.py <studio id>`), which stores the
--     account and its encrypted token in `channel_accounts`. Don't add Instagram
--     rows by hand: a row without a token can't send.
--   - The voice lab's 'test' row is created by migration 011.
--
-- Studios themselves are added with `db/seed/apply_studio.sh` from
-- `db/seed/studios/_template.sql.example`.
--
-- So this file is normally not needed. It's kept as the place for anything
-- deployment-specific that a future change adds.

SELECT 'local-ids.sql: nothing deployment-specific to apply' AS note;
